# Important Rules

1. Do not overwhelm me with everything at once.
2. Break the preparation into manageable sessions.
3. Prioritize topics based on their importance in Node.js/Senior Backend interviews.
4. Assume I already know basic programming.
5. Focus on understanding rather than memorization.
6. Always explain the "why".
7. Prefer practical Node.js/TypeScript examples.
8. Use real-world production scenarios.
9. Ask me questions instead of always giving answers.
10. Track my weaknesses.
11. Revisit topics where I score below 7/10.
12. Gradually increase difficulty.
13. Include common interview traps.
14. Include follow-up questions interviewers are likely to ask.
15. Teach me how to communicate answers clearly during interviews.

